# todos: the examples/todos app under a real pty (gate).
#
# The app renders a styled "Todos" header whose tail is a live state needle
# "n=<total> d=<done> k=<keys>" — k is a per-key counter, so every frame's
# needle is unique and each expect is deterministic (no stale-substring match).
# Flows proven end-to-end:
#   * add: type "buy milk" (spaces included) + enter -> n=0..1
#   * add again: "eggs" + enter -> n=1..2
#   * toggle done: x on the selected (first) todo -> d=0..1
#   * filter: "/" enters filter mode, "milk" shrinks the list, enter applies
#     (the header needle is stable through the filter lifecycle)
#   * clear filter: esc (applied filter -> cleared, not quit)
#   * clear done: C drops the done "buy milk" -> n=2..1
#   * delete: d drops the selected "eggs" -> n=1..0
#   * quit: q -> show cursor (\e[?25h) + exit 0
#
# Escapes: \e[?25l hide cursor, \e[?25h show cursor, \x1b esc, \r enter.
expect n=0 d=0 k=0
send buy milk
expect n=0 d=0 k=8
send \r
expect n=1 d=0 k=9
send eggs
expect n=1 d=0 k=13
send \r
expect n=2 d=0 k=14
send x
expect n=2 d=1 k=15
send /
expect n=2 d=1 k=16
send milk
expect n=2 d=1 k=20
send \r
expect n=2 d=1 k=21
send \x1b
expect n=2 d=1 k=22
send C
expect n=1 d=0 k=23
send d
expect n=0 d=0 k=24
send q
expect \e[?25h
expect_exit 0
